381053 1145 "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nIn this case, since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Q(x)‖ & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{6})}^{2}} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381055 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381056 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381057 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381058 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381059 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1041 "selection" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381058 13194139536050 true] [17592186381054 1110 #uuid "b2e871d6-82d8-5e94-b3cc-3c21ef69a415" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381055 1034 "4\\sqrt{6}" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381055 1111 #uuid "1d4373db-d69f-509f-b61a-9df6545acd6b" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381056 1034 "7\\sqrt{2}" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381056 1111 #uuid "02f82e33-327d-5475-b8a5-804644130bb4" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381057 1034 "6" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381057 1111 #uuid "fc58a63c-67b1-53a6-bdee-629b4ae3bc44" 131941