\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nIn this case, since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x)\\cdot Q(y) & =x\\cdot y \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381090 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381091 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381092 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381093 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381094 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1041 "selection" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381093 13194139536050 true] [17592186381089 1110 #uuid "9836f3fe-c18e-5a3e-b917-431206b4367d" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381090 1034 "10" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381090 1111 #uuid "267b21ee-4b46-5539-9137-61f80c5d3600" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381091 1034 "6" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381091 1111 #uuid "6f0be104-0d5c-547e-9a31-19b04b9c3f69" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381092 1034 "-3" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381092 1111 #uuid "778720aa-11b6-5fbe-9b0e-f69c1959b59f" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381093 1034 "0" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536050 true] [17592186381093 1111 #uuid "a52420d0-1bd7-5619-ac3b-89b927b82e42" 13194139536050 true] [17592186381094 1034 "-1" 131941395360